--TEST--
Core\IO::read and Core\IO::write refuse every spelling of a path with no grant behind it — counted over a sweep of relative, dotted, nested and parent-walking forms rather than read off one line, so a door that resolved one spelling into an allowance still fails here — `rule:security/capability-question-is-grant-and-scope` and `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A refusal asserted one path at a time is a refusal a member can pass by
// answering plausibly for the path in the case. The claim is the *invariant* --
// with nothing granted, no spelling is readable and none is writable -- so the
// sweep is counted and the counts are what print. A door that let a single form
// through moves a number here whatever it printed for the others.
//
// The forms are the ones a path arrives in: bare, dot-prefixed, nested, and one
// walking out through `..`, which is the spelling `rule:security/path-scope-canonicalise-then-prefix`'s canonicalise-
// then-prefix rule exists for once a root *is* granted. Each is joined onto this
// file's folder while the program runs, so the door is handed every form whole
// and absolute, `..` included.
class Here {
    public static function path(#[Core\Path] string $path): string {
        return $path;
    }
}
string $dir = Here::path('.');
array<string> $paths = [
    "notes.txt",
    "./notes.txt",
    "docs/notes.txt",
    "../notes.txt",
    "../../etc/notes.txt",
];
int $total = Core\Arr::count($paths) as int;

int $readsRefused = 0;
int $readsNamingFsRead = 0;
int $writesRefused = 0;
int $writesNamingFsWrite = 0;

int $i = 0;
for (; $i < $total; $i = $i + 1) {
    string $path = Core\Path::join($dir, $paths[$i]);

    try {
        string $content = Core\IO::read($path);
    } catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
        $readsRefused = $readsRefused + 1;
        // The capability's own name, in the spelling `nvs.toml` grants it
        // under, is what an operator pastes into a file -- so it is counted
        // rather than assumed from the fact that something threw.
        if ($refused->message == "Core\\IO::read needs the capability `fs.read` for " . $path . ", which is not granted\nhelp: grant it in nvs.toml under `[capabilities.fs]`") {
            $readsNamingFsRead = $readsNamingFsRead + 1;
        }
    }

    try {
        Core\IO::write($path, "x");
    } catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
        $writesRefused = $writesRefused + 1;
        if ($refused->message == "Core\\IO::write needs the capability `fs.write` for " . $path . ", which is not granted\nhelp: grant it in nvs.toml under `[capabilities.fs]`") {
            $writesNamingFsWrite = $writesNamingFsWrite + 1;
        }
    }
}

echo "paths: ", $total as string, "\n";
echo "reads refused: ", $readsRefused as string, ", naming fs.read: ", $readsNamingFsRead as string, "\n";
echo "writes refused: ", $writesRefused as string, ", naming fs.write: ", $writesNamingFsWrite as string, "\n";
--EXPECT--
paths: 5
reads refused: 5, naming fs.read: 5
writes refused: 5, naming fs.write: 5
